{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861652-do-solars-need-a-sifu","id":861652,"title":"Do Solars Need a Sifu?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-08T00:10:04-07:00","id":861652,"title":"Do Solars Need a Sifu?","content":"Okay this has been cropping up a lot lately and it's actually going to be pertinent to my game soon, since a player wants to start teaching himself single point. In the past Solars have been able to learn martial arts just like any other charm, they can develop whole styles totally independent of being taught them. I mean heck I'm pretty sure you were allowed to teach yourself tiger style even if your character lived in the far south and had never even SEEN a tiger.<br /> <br /> One of my dawns is a master of white reaper and finds his single opponent skills lacking so he wants to just buy a sword and start swinging away until he generates Single Point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T00:12:40-07:00","id":861654,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'm not sure you were allowed to teach yourself Tiger style. Otherwise, what would be the point of all those Martial Arts schools? It seems genre-inappropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T00:16:23-07:00","id":861655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861652-do-solars-need-a-sifu?p=861654#post861654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I'm not sure you were allowed to teach yourself Tiger style. Otherwise, what would be the point of all those Martial Arts schools? It seems genre-inappropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but, somebody made up tiger style, right? That dude didn't need a teacher. Also didn't 2e specify that SMA were special because even though Solars could learn them they needed a sidereal teacher to do so? Implying they didn't need a teacher for other styles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T00:19:53-07:00","id":861656,"title":"","content":"Like with everything else in the game and in the real world, it's easier to benefit from the knowledge of another than it is to invent it or discover it all by yourself. I'd rule that a Solar is just fine learning all but the most esoteric (for instance, Sidereal-made or developed in a paradigm divorced from yours, such as a style native to the Wyld or the Underworld or Autochthonia) of martial arts styles on his own, though of course he'll do it faster under the tutelage of a sifu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T00:28:34-07:00","id":861657,"title":"","content":"You can find the style manual by chance, a character find the instruction for Bei Ming Shen Gong in one of Jin Yong's novel by bowing before a statue so many time that the pillow under the statue got torn, revealing the manual inside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T00:51:39-07:00","id":861668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861652-do-solars-need-a-sifu#post861652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my dawns is a master of white reaper and finds his single opponent skills lacking so he wants to just buy a sword and start swinging away until he generates Single Point.</div> </div> </div> </div>If a Dawn just starts 'swinging away' in an attempt to be a better sword fighter, the result is him getting Melee charms.<br /> <br /> Solar charms are supernatural expressions of ability. Martial arts are specific, codified styles that involve manipulating your essence in a way that is not natural. They are not intuitive.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T01:35:43-07:00","id":861681,"title":"","content":"I was under the impression that the only Style Solars didn't need a teacher for in Second Edition was Snake. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but, somebody made up tiger style, right? That dude didn't need a teacher.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is so tautological I don't even know how to begin refuting it coherently. I mean, by that logic, why ever bother learning anything from anybody? I'm sure we all have enough Einstein in us to independently develop theories of Relativity, right? That's how developing things works, yes? Hey, why even bother reading the Exalted books? Grabowski didn't need anybody to write a book for him, did he?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T01:52:19-07:00","id":861689,"title":"","content":"Assuming they do need a sifu, who would they go to? Apart from other Solars (who may potentially need an unbroken line of sifus back to the first age, where the style was more common), who could know and demonstrate Solar-level competences in the arts?<br /> <br /> I<br /> Although, saying that, I seem to remember that mortals can now learn the same basic art as an Exalted, they just don't have the additional mojo to leverage the essence manipulation Solars engage in. In that case, a mortal could teach it. The Solar's essence channelling naturally adds superior effects, like geomancy for the body; you can build a manse anywhere, but it'll only tap its power if it's on the proper ley line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T01:54:59-07:00","id":861690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861652-do-solars-need-a-sifu#post861652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay this has been cropping up a lot lately and it's actually going to be pertinent to my game soon, since a player wants to start teaching himself single point. In the past Solars have been able to learn martial arts just like any other charm, they can develop whole styles totally independent of being taught them. I mean heck I'm pretty sure you were allowed to teach yourself tiger style even if your character lived in the far south and had never even SEEN a tiger.<br /> <br /> One of my dawns is a master of white reaper and finds his single opponent skills lacking so he wants to just buy a sword and start swinging away until he generates Single Point.</div> </div> </div> </div>If he just swings his sword wildly, yeah he get solar melee not Single Point.<br /> <br /> If the starts to &quot;science the shit out of&quot; every swing he makes and how he can focus his essence on single purpose, minimize and reach perfection in each of his swings, he can invent Single Point.<br /> so it depends on the stunt.<br /> <br /> Also he can always just remember how to &quot;Single Point&quot; with a flashback. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Solars only need a sifu for sidereal martial arts, anything less can be learned by effort, it just takes more time. &quot;<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2-Roman\">Mentors and similarly skilled trainers should also reduce training times, proportionate to their skill at teaching. </span></span>&quot; p.178, Ex3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":910,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","user":"Ncolic","date":". 04-08-2016, 04:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/910-ncolic","name":"Ncolic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T01:57:02-07:00","id":861691,"title":"","content":"Wait... this Edition treats Martial Arts differently... a Solar probably needs a teacher to learn the Style, but not the Charms (even though the described training method for the Charms is different from that of Solar Charms), since the idea of the Charms is that it's the Style as it would be practiced by an Exalt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T01:57:06-07:00","id":861692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861652-do-solars-need-a-sifu?p=861681#post861681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was under the impression that the only Style Solars didn't need a teacher for in Second Edition was Snake. This is so tautological I don't even know how to begin refuting it coherently. I mean, by that logic, why ever bother learning anything from anybody? I'm sure we all have enough Einstein in us to independently develop theories of Relativity, right? That's how developing things works, yes? Hey, why even bother reading the Exalted books? Grabowski didn't need anybody to write a book for him, did he?!</div> </div> </div> </div>We're talking about a solar exalt with supernal martial arts here, as far as MA is concerned he IS Einstein. There is literally nobody in the universe more qualified to develop a martial art wholesale from scratch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T02:02:58-07:00","id":861695,"title":"","content":"Although to be fair I have three other players who are planning on learning their own MA styles and none of them want a sifu either, also none of them are dawns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T02:29:21-07:00","id":861701,"title":"","content":"Well someone must've created the Martial Art at some point. They don't just appear out of thin air in an old wise mentor conveniently. So....yeah, I'd say its possible, otherwise the Martial Art would never have been invented in the first place. Given that these are techniques, its possible to develop them independently because they have a structure that can be recognized.<br /> <br /> that and to my headcanon, most martial arts styles actually do survive through mortals just practicing the basic movements. its just that Exalting unlocks the real potential for said style, much like enlightenment. of course if all else fails, you just have to put in a Conveniently Placed School of Martial Arts if really need one, because Gold Faction Sidereals got your back y'know what I mean?<br /> <br /> because I'm sure a Sidereal can go &quot;hey, the Solar is trying to learn Single Point, I'll just do a little adjustment of fate here and there and presto...on his way to the nearest place to learn.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6018-raziere","name":"Raziere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6018_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T02:45:28-07:00","id":861707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861652-do-solars-need-a-sifu?p=861692#post861692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're talking about a solar exalt with supernal martial arts here, as far as MA is concerned he IS Einstein. There is literally nobody in the universe more qualified to develop a martial art wholesale from scratch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Einstein didn't develop the theory of relativity by &quot;just buying a chalkboard and tossing numbers on it until mathematical equations popped out.&quot; He received a solid education and had a four-year degree in mathematics and physics at one of the best universities in the world. Even though he was 17 when he entered university, he didn't publish &quot;A New Determination of Molecular Dimensions&quot; until he was 26.<br /> <br /> If your players want to develop martial arts, the idea is that they treat it as a serious undertaking. They need to work on it as they would any major project, and it should fulfill the narrative of a dedicated martial artist discovering and refining this new fighting style.<br /> <br /> If they just want it for the cool charms, then create an old man on a mountain top they'll need to learn it from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T02:58:10-07:00","id":861714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861652-do-solars-need-a-sifu#post861652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my dawns is a master of white reaper and finds his single opponent skills lacking so he wants to just buy a sword and start swinging away until he generates Single Point.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>&quot;I had no idea where he came from. The swordsman simply appeared in the middle of the forest, when I was practicing my strikes. He wore full-body robes, and had a straw hat... And then he drew his sword in one smooth motion, bisecting a leaf in midair. He turned to face me after he sheathed his blade, and though he said nothing, I know what he wanted me to do.<br /> <br /> &quot;I don't know how long I practiced, but he was patient and reassuring, correcting me on how to properly draw and strike. When the moon began to set over Creation, he bowed to me before he vanished into the forest.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> &quot;And that's how you picked up your first dot of Single Point Style.&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: I double-checked the Corebook... Says that a dot of a Caste or Favored ability will take about [New Rank] days, so by that guideline it'll take about a day to build up your first dot of Single Point Style, if you have MA Caste or Favored. I assume this Dawn does. And it says that a sufficient tutor can indeed reduce training times, such as a Sidereal appearing in the middle of the night to teach a wayward Solar how to use the Single Point Style. So yeah, one night of training would PROBABLY be enough to justify that first dot, and the rest afterwards can be &quot;I'm practicing what I know and improving it&quot; to justify the additional dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 04-08-2016, 06:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T03:08:13-07:00","id":861717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raziere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861652-do-solars-need-a-sifu?p=861701#post861701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that and to my headcanon, most martial arts styles actually do survive through mortals just practicing the basic movements. its just that Exalting unlocks the real potential for said style, much like enlightenment.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not headcanon in 3ed. It is bookcanon. The exalt learns the same moves mortals do and then makes them awesome.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T03:10:27-07:00","id":861719,"title":"","content":"I'm of the opinion that even a Solar needs to learn a new Style from a sifu. You can make that aspect as big or small as you like, ranging from (as Kyman so flavourfully examplified above) teaching the first dot in the Style and then letting the Solar either find a new teacher or develop more dots herself, to staying with a single master who'll instruct in both the mortal and supernatural aspects of the Style.<br /> <br /> 'd lean more towards letting Solars learn Charms without a teacher than dots without a teacher, myself. Honestly, it's not hard to contrive a teaching situation. An established school, random people in the woods, your own Past Lives... it's worth it to keep the idea of the martial arts world alive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T05:04:11-07:00","id":861748,"title":"","content":"Worth noting, I think, that even in 1e and 2e there were no guidelines for &quot;inventing&quot; Styles I can recall. The Solar capacity for being self-taught was atributed to remembering a Style a previous holder of your Exaltation knew. Snake was called our as having been so ubiquitous in the First Age that basically every Solar Martial Artist knew it and thus any modern Solar could &quot;remember&quot; it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T05:10:56-07:00","id":861752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861652-do-solars-need-a-sifu?p=861719#post861719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm of the opinion that even a Solar needs to learn a new Style from a sifu. You can make that aspect as big or small as you like, ranging from (as Kyman so flavourfully examplified above) teaching the first dot in the Style and then letting the Solar either find a new teacher or develop more dots herself, to staying with a single master who'll instruct in both the mortal and supernatural aspects of the Style.<br /> <br /> 'd lean more towards letting Solars learn Charms without a teacher than dots without a teacher, myself. Honestly, it's not hard to contrive a teaching situation. An established school, random people in the woods, your own Past Lives... it's worth it to keep the idea of the martial arts world alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's how I'd do it (and, well, do do it). You must have a teacher/some ancient texts to learn a style (as in the dots) but the charms you don't.<br /> <br /> Of course, I hand out style tutors and texts to the PCs like candy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T06:46:08-07:00","id":861792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861652-do-solars-need-a-sifu?p=861752#post861752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course, I hand out style tutors and texts to the PCs like candy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they may need a tutor, but the ST shouldn't make it too difficult to find one. It also gives the PCs a connection to someone in the world. After learning spending time a Martial Arts style from someone, you are going to develop some sort of intimacy for them (either good or bad). <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T07:39:36-07:00","id":861824,"title":"","content":"I suspect that anyone in the setting requires a Sifu in order to learn 1) The Merit for the first time, and 2) The ability dots associated with each specific martial art. In keeping with the flavor, I firmly believe the charms should be figured out for themselves as they apply their essence to the techniques they are taught. In this case, techniques are flavor representations of your ability dots. Once you have Martial Arts (Tiger Style) 5, you shouldn't need a Sifu.<br /> <br /> My 2 cents.<br /> <br /> Also<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861652-do-solars-need-a-sifu?p=861655#post861655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also didn't 2e specify that SMA were special because even though Solars could learn them they needed a sidereal teacher to do so? Implying they didn't need a teacher for other styles.</div> </div> </div> </div>What this implies is that a Solar who knows SMA can't teach another Solar SMA. Only a Sidereal can teach SMA to a Solar. It doesn't really imply anything about non-SMA martial arts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T07:39:50-07:00","id":861825,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I suppose I could go the texts route, or the past lives one. I think the main thing is none of them want to be beholden to a Sifu, especially the dawn, who believes that nobody has any authority greater than his.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T07:48:15-07:00","id":861829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861652-do-solars-need-a-sifu?p=861824#post861824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect that anyone in the setting requires a Sifu in order to learn 1) The Merit for the first time, and 2) The ability dots associated with each specific martial art. In keeping with the flavor, I firmly believe the charms should be figured out for themselves as they apply their essence to the techniques they are taught. In this case, techniques are flavor representations of your ability dots. Once you have Martial Arts (Tiger Style) 5, you shouldn't need a Sifu.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this. If a mortal sifu can teach you the techniques and you can figure out the charms from there then you don't need the mortal sifu for the charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T08:14:50-07:00","id":861845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861652-do-solars-need-a-sifu?p=861825#post861825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think the main thing is none of them want to be beholden to a Sifu, especially the dawn, who believes that nobody has any authority greater than his.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on how much you want to give him what he wants and how much you want to say &quot;too bad, that's not how it works,&quot; if only for plot value.<br /> <br /> Honestly I find the sentiment of the Dawn exceptionally off-putting, so I'd probably go the latter, because to me it makes for a more interesting story if a full-of-himself asshole has to actually admit someone might know more from him and he can learn from them, and might create some interesting moments. To me that arc is more interesting than simply giving them exactly what they want. YMMV.<br /> <br /> In general, I say you need a sifu or a style manual at least for the mundane dots, and the Charms can be expressed by someone with the proper training, as long as they have awakened Essence. I'm not sure how this meshes with how I feel the IMA should work and the stories about mortal monks who become Solars etc, but that's neither here nor there for this thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 04-08-2016, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T08:15:13-07:00","id":861846,"title":"","content":"<i>Need</i>? Probably not, but it would cut down on training times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T08:17:49-07:00","id":861847,"title":"","content":"I'm going to chime in just a personal preference. One of the concepts i'd like to play (that works easiest obviously with a dawn) that can work for any Exalt, is one seeking a mortal sifu for training. Really any sifu will do, but I do like the idea of an exalt calling a mortal master and deferring to them. I like the idea that while their charms are mighty, they can still be taught by a mortal. Just my two cents on this subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T09:01:38-07:00","id":861874,"title":"","content":"Way things go in 3e, with each martial art style being a skill all its own and <b>then</b> powered up by exalted awesomeness, i would say yes, you need a sifu to teach you the essentials, though it is perfectly acceptable for a character to have learned the mundane forms of the style before exalting and then &quot;re-teaching&quot; itself into the supernatural strata on its own or to glean bits and pieces of its past self as a weird and somewhat unreliable sifu.<br /> <br /> Developing a whole style from zero? Honestly not, unless the character <b>already</b> possesses the MA and Essence levels required to develop all the charms of the style beforehand, supernal MA be damned. So no &quot;self-taught master&quot; hijinks before Essence 3 at least. YMMV, but that's mostly how i would roll with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T09:21:17-07:00","id":861893,"title":"","content":"It's helpful to read the actual rules here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mentors and similarly skilled trainers should also reduce training times, proportionate to their skill at teaching. </div> </div> </div>So, by default, training times given represent the time to self-develop your own skills.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally, a word on advancing mystical traits. While it is possible to give instruction in Charms, most Chosen, and certainly most Solars, develop their own Charms through instinctive cultivation of skill rather than through rigorous practice. As such, while Charms can certainly be trained like any other skill, many characters 'train' their Charms by exercising the Ability in question under duress. Evocations usually require extensive training with the Artifact they're attached to, but also demand that the Exalt establish a rapport with his equipment, often on the field of battle. Martial Arts Charms always require rigorous training, and learning spells requires a mentor or a text copy of the spell in question and many hours of intense study. </div> </div> </div>So, look: <i>only</i> spells are called out as requiring external instruction. Martial arts charms are explicitly listed <i>without</i> that constraint - self-training is entirely possible, it's just that you can't say &quot;poof I know new charm&quot; you have to claim you have been explicitly working on learning a new charm. But very very clearly you do not require external instruction for it.<br /> <br /> If I were to, <i>as a house-rule</i>, apply any kind of training requirements to Martial Arts, it would solely apply to learning the first dot of a new style, and I'd permit that to be learned from text rather than from a sifu. A sifu will surely be helpful, but once you &quot;know&quot; a style, even at the one-dot level, there is no good reason that a Solar Exalt especially couldn't train by himself to pefect his own mastery of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T09:28:02-07:00","id":861898,"title":"","content":"If the players doesn't want to go through the narrative elements of a relationship with a teacher I wouldn't force it (unless you've established that in your version of Creation that's how things work, period). The guy doesn't actually need to learn &quot;Single Point Shining into the Void&quot; unless it's important to the story that it be called that. As long as it makes sense for the character to create a martial art (which is seems like it does since he's already a master of at least one) then an extended scene of him experimenting with a sword and laying the ground work for a new style designed for single combat would be cool.<br /> <br /> That actually opens up a lot of interesting stories if he later runs across somebody else who happens to use a very similar style of combat. How did someone else learn something that he invented out in the woods, alone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T09:46:58-07:00","id":861917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861652-do-solars-need-a-sifu?p=861825#post861825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I suppose I could go the texts route, or the past lives one. I think the main thing is none of them want to be beholden to a Sifu, especially the dawn, who believes that nobody has any authority greater than his.</div> </div> </div> </div>But isn't that more awesome that he thinks so. As a GM I do not try and punish players for who their character is. But if u do not want to have a master, someone who can teach you quicker than texts or self teaching. It should be hard. That's the choice he made. It makes cool drama. A dawn who can take out nearly everything in existence having to humble himself to a weak old man. Isn't that what exalted is about? That u have the power to do anything but not the knowledge? Isn't the tropes of Kung Fu mastery of the mind and spirit not just the fist. Learning to be humble plays a part in mystical martial arts. learning a new style is starting at square one. It doesn't matter if ur the best fighter in creation. That no one can beat u. When you learn a new style u will have to fight everyone else in that Soho in that style, not the one u already mastered. And u might loose more than u win at first. Sitting there looking knowibg u could win if you pitted ur style against theirs. But as long as u think like that u will never move on and learn the new style. You must forget everything you know. <br /> <br /> The game is made to have fun but you must also be fair to the world. Marital arts have power in creation even got morals. No matter what exalt you are the styles are the same. From my experience something early means more than something freely given. <br /> Learning a new style should be a plot point. If he tries to recreate it, certain Soho's will not like that he is bastardised their style. If he is going to look for texts of the style he will have to search creation. Price to be worthy of the text from the owner. Or do a favour for him, or steal it. I would even split the texts in 3 books. One that goes from 1-2 dots, 2nd 3-4 etc. I wouldn't make them hard to get but I would make it seem hard to get in game, as these must be rare. Make it half to a full session to get. Make them know it will he quicker to have a teacher and even quicker with the texts and a teacher. <br /> Baaicly make it fun to start learning it. Out of game he wants to do better with single targets. In game it should mean more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4090-mental-state","name":"Mental-State","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T09:57:53-07:00","id":861925,"title":"","content":"Oh for r creating your own style I would say you would have to finish mastering the mundane elements before the supernatural elements. So you would Have to finish creating the style (getting 5 dots) to the take it further. You would have to fnish style you then have insight how it all fits together.<br /> That's how enlightenment works. Once you have gained it realise that you really only know a drop and to start learning again. <br /> Here is a half remembered Bruce Lee quote. <br /> Before I learned to fight I thought a punch was just a punch and a kick was just a kick. Once I mastered fighting I realised a punch is just a punch and a kick is just a kick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4090-mental-state","name":"Mental-State","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T10:11:21-07:00","id":861934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861652-do-solars-need-a-sifu?p=861681#post861681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was under the impression that the only Style Solars didn't need a teacher for in Second Edition was Snake. This is so tautological I don't even know how to begin refuting it coherently. I mean, by that logic, why ever bother learning anything from anybody? I'm sure we all have enough Einstein in us to independently develop theories of Relativity, right? That's how developing things works, yes? Hey, why even bother reading the Exalted books? Grabowski didn't need anybody to write a book for him, did he?!</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, never forget exalts are kinda like the guys that excel on that level. If there is someone out there inventing knowledge out of seemingly nowhere (even when it isn't, looking at you einstein and newton and maxwell, you bastard triat) these are the guys who'll do it.<br /> <br /> But back at the whole thing.<br /> Obviously someone inventing the style without a particular intent to do so is bullshit. But there's nothing against inventing a style. You just kinda need to, well, want to. you want a prettier way of saying it? Life itself is your sifu. Emulate the tiger, study the way the wind swirls around crevices and obstacles, Erase your presence until there is no thought, only action. Or amplify it until where there was enemy intent to oppose you, there is only your overwhelming power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 04-08-2016, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T11:12:35-07:00","id":861984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861652-do-solars-need-a-sifu?p=861655#post861655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah but, somebody made up tiger style, right? That dude didn't need a teacher. Also didn't 2e specify that SMA were special because even though Solars could learn them they needed a sidereal teacher to do so? Implying they didn't need a teacher for other styles.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That person had most assuredly seen a tiger, tho lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T11:15:43-07:00","id":861985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861652-do-solars-need-a-sifu?p=861984#post861984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That person had most assuredly seen a tiger, tho lol</div> </div> </div> </div>I tend to assume given the obnoxious level of Southern wealth that quite a few rulers would keep a menagerie filled with impressive things (that won't ultra-murder you for trying to capture them) like tigers, lion, elephants, patricians, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T11:16:08-07:00","id":861986,"title":"","content":"To address the basic question of the thread: Yes, Martial Arts are specific schools with particular techniques and methodologies and you need some source to learn from, be it a sifu or a training manual or even unusually detailed folk legends, whatever, unless you are trying to create your own style. Luckily, teachers are not nearly so hard to come by in this edition since very few styles are restricted to practice by the Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T11:25:21-07:00","id":861997,"title":"","content":"Something I would also accept for a Solar trying to learn a new MA style:<br /> <br /> &quot;Ugh, I don't know WHAT that guy was doing with his sword, but he was GOOD. Man... Huh, wonder if I can do that.&quot; *Practices drawing their sword rapidly for an entire day*<br /> <br /> (I think that a Solar learning by taking the Style head-on and remembering the basics from the fight is perfectly acceptable)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T11:28:29-07:00","id":862002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861652-do-solars-need-a-sifu?p=861986#post861986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To address the basic question of the thread: Yes, Martial Arts are specific schools with particular techniques and methodologies and you need some source to learn from, be it a sifu or a training manual or even unusually detailed folk legends, whatever, unless you are trying to create your own style. Luckily, teachers are not nearly so hard to come by in this edition since very few styles are restricted to practice by the Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the sifu covered by the MA merit or do you have to buy a mentor? <br /> <br /> (I assume if you want your sifu to do more than teach MA, he will need to be a mentor or ally)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T11:40:58-07:00","id":862015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861652-do-solars-need-a-sifu?p=861997#post861997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something I would also accept for a Solar trying to learn a new MA style:<br /> <br /> &quot;Ugh, I don't know WHAT that guy was doing with his sword, but he was GOOD. Man... Huh, wonder if I can do that.&quot; *Practices drawing their sword rapidly for an entire day*<br /> <br /> (I think that a Solar learning by taking the Style head-on and remembering the basics from the fight is perfectly acceptable)</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I'd make it edge case. That's effectively the same as trying to &quot;recreate&quot; the Style, rather than getting instruction. It'd be the same as trying to learn Tiger Style by watching a tiger, that is, creating it from scratch.<br /> <br /> If the table climate leans that way, then I'd consider it, but it doesn't really capture the idea of tutorship that I'd like it to have. Of course, it's entirely possible for someone to want to <i>teach</i> a Style by showing the business end of it, but that's another thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T11:45:44-07:00","id":862021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861652-do-solars-need-a-sifu?p=862015#post862015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I'd make it edge case. That's effectively the same as trying to &quot;recreate&quot; the Style, rather than getting instruction. It'd be the same as trying to learn Tiger Style by watching a tiger, that is, creating it from scratch.<br /> <br /> If the table climate leans that way, then I'd consider it, but it doesn't really capture the idea of tutorship that I'd like it to have. Of course, it's entirely possible for someone to want to <i>teach</i> a Style by showing the business end of it, but that's another thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, it would depend on the mood of the table. And I'd sooner have my PCs be guided to a mortal Sifu, or as I mentioned on the first page, have a mysterious person show up and give them lessons in secret. Hell, even finding an instructional scroll would be more likely to be accepted.<br /> <br /> Still, just tossing out ideas to see if any stick.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861652-do-solars-need-a-sifu?p=862002#post862002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is the sifu covered by the MA merit or do you have to buy a mentor?<br /> <br /> (I assume if you want your sifu to do more than teach MA, he will need to be a mentor or ally)</div> </div> </div> </div>If I were ST, I'd rule that if you bought the MA Merit you <i>had</i> a Sifu. You might even run into them again at some point in your adventure. But if you want to say &quot;Hey, my old Sifu might be willing to give us shelter for the night&quot; without needing to use a Social Influence roll (even if it's easy peasy because the old coot still has an Intimacy for their former student) then yes, you'd need to invest in them as a Mentor or an Ally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 04-08-2016, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T12:38:42-07:00","id":862088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861652-do-solars-need-a-sifu?p=862021#post862021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were ST, I'd rule that if you bought the MA Merit you <i>had</i> a Sifu. You might even run into them again at some point in your adventure. But if you want to say &quot;Hey, my old Sifu might be willing to give us shelter for the night&quot; without needing to use a Social Influence roll (even if it's easy peasy because the old coot still has an Intimacy for their former student) then yes, you'd need to invest in them as a Mentor or an Ally.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is how I'd house rule it too. Though you would have to buy an additional Merit for your Sifu if you want him to be more than some old dude living in a humble cottage, a hermit in living in a tree, or a tiger! (I like that idea). Like if he was a master of a major MA school or a respected leader of the community.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T12:55:19-07:00","id":862108,"title":"","content":"Well the mentor merit also implies at how powerful or skilled your mentor is, so you could argue that a sifu is included in the martial arts merit just not one of any great significance. Basically your teacher isn't anyone of any great significance outside of the dojo, or their academy. The mentor also probably wouldn't be too willing to put itself out for your character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T13:01:07-07:00","id":862118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861652-do-solars-need-a-sifu?p=862088#post862088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is how I'd house rule it too. Though you would have to buy an additional Merit for your Sifu if you want him to be more than some old dude living in a humble cottage, a hermit in living in a tree, or a tiger! (I like that idea). Like if he was a master of a major MA school or a respected leader of the community.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;And this is my Sifu. She took me in as a child and taught me how to properly use the Tiger Style.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://vignette3.wikia.nocookie.net/kungfupanda/images/a/ab/Tigresspose.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20110407180332\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;... Er... Um... I can see she's clearly a master?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh yeah, she is.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T12:45:43-07:00","id":863273,"title":"","content":"This is how I would solve the problem. Have your player seek out a dojo where a sensei teaches single point style and have that person teach your boy the style. Even if the sensei is a mortal he still knows the techniques (charms) of the style, which the exalted then learn. I'm of the opionion that exalted aren't limited to rare exalted kung fu masters just so he can be better at what his character is all about. I see martial arts charms as the names of techniques that make up a style, mortals can &quot;learn&quot; them, but can't fully unlock their true power.<br /> There your boy can learn bad-ass swordsmenship now. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1131-hyper-prime","name":"Hyper Prime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1131_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T13:43:10-07:00","id":863302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hyper Prime</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861652-do-solars-need-a-sifu?p=863273#post863273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There your boy can learn bad-ass swordsmenship now. :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently the Dawn's player doesn't want to &quot;be beholden to a Sifu&quot;. And if that came up at my table, admittedly, my reaction would be to look the player in the eyes and say &quot;Well tough titties&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T14:10:23-07:00","id":863325,"title":"","content":"This is that episode of last airbender isn't it? Sokka's Master? That was good stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T14:28:27-07:00","id":863331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861652-do-solars-need-a-sifu?p=863302#post863302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Apparently the Dawn's player doesn't want to &quot;be beholden to a Sifu&quot;. And if that came up at my table, admittedly, my reaction would be to look the player in the eyes and say &quot;Well tough titties&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless his arrogance was diminishing everyone's enjoyment, why not let him have his character?<br /> <br /> Supreme Warrior Who Always Does Shit His Own Way is not a stretch for a Dawn.<br /> <br /> You could go with the developer's intent as stated by Holden above and introduce a folk tale about a swordsman who could kill you without you even seeing the blade leave the scabbard. Let him look for the wise old man who knows the details of the story in the village five valleys over. Let them have a chat and then he can start on his discovery of the Style.<br /> <br /> I also seem to remember that the fluff on certain Martial Arts even indicate that they are the &quot;true expression&quot; of that skill, like Single Point is the unheard in generations true form of Invisible Blade in the Wind Style and Glimpse of the Edge Style. So there is a story for the Dawn, who sees these lesser styles being practiced by his enemies and brings Single Point back into the world.<br /> <br /> It is a good thing to, as a ST, take stories you don't particularly like but that a player enjoys and try to make it work for the whole table. As long as no one is being a prick, why be one yourself?<br /> <br /> As AtG stated, nothing in RAW indicates apprenticeship as a requirement, sufficiently able mentors reduce training times, so it could be assumed that the training times already given are for self development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T15:18:55-07:00","id":863346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/861652-do-solars-need-a-sifu?p=863331#post863331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless his arrogance was diminishing everyone's enjoyment, why not let him have his character?<br /> <br /> Supreme Warrior Who Always Does Shit His Own Way is not a stretch for a Dawn.<br /> <br /> You could go with the developer's intent as stated by Holden above and introduce a folk tale about a swordsman who could kill you without you even seeing the blade leave the scabbard. Let him look for the wise old man who knows the details of the story in the village five valleys over. Let them have a chat and then he can start on his discovery of the Style.<br /> <br /> I also seem to remember that the fluff on certain Martial Arts even indicate that they are the &quot;true expression&quot; of that skill, like Single Point is the unheard in generations true form of Invisible Blade in the Wind Style and Glimpse of the Edge Style. So there is a story for the Dawn, who sees these lesser styles being practiced by his enemies and brings Single Point back into the world.<br /> <br /> It is a good thing to, as a ST, take stories you don't particularly like but that a player enjoys and try to make it work for the whole table. As long as no one is being a prick, why be one yourself?<br /> <br /> As AtG stated, nothing in RAW indicates apprenticeship as a requirement, sufficiently able mentors reduce training times, so it could be assumed that the training times already given are for self development.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll give you that, and I guess I was more looking at the &quot;I want to develop it on my own&quot;<br /> <br /> Lost scrolls are great, as are folkstories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-10T15:50:59-07:00","id":863364,"title":"","content":"I see, problem wasn't for the dawn to find a sensei... OK if he wants to invent his own version of single point shinning then let him battle a hundred foes with a slashing sword not using neither his melee or martial arts charms. These battles must be must be one on one fights. Once this &quot;quest&quot; has been completed (meaning he survived it), then he can spend the XP for the martial arts merrit for single point shinning (??), he then gives it a cool new name. From this point on when he wants to learn a new &quot;single point shinning&quot; style charm he must follow the rules for inventing new charms. There BOOM! Your boy is a legendary bad-ass. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1131-hyper-prime","name":"Hyper Prime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1131_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}